    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green, including the new `coreRejectsIdentityCollision`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nDuplicate detection is now a single derived key: `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`, and a create is rejected 409 only when the **whole** key matches an existing owner.\n\n**New, small, cohesive units** (each with near-zero surrounding complexity):\n- `CheckUniqueIdentity` \u2014 one `service` step that scans owners and throws on a full-key collision, plus a static `identityKey(Owner)` helper that is the single source of truth for the derivation.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException` (checked) + `DuplicateIdentityHandler` (\u2192 409) + its escalation YAML, mirroring the existing duplicate-handler pattern.\n\n**Rewiring** `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Moved `assignHousehold` to run right after `build`, so `householdId` is populated *before* the key is computed.\n- Replaced the three steps `checkTelephone` / `checkEmail` / `checkHousehold` with the one `checkIdentity` step (using `method: service` since the class exposes the shared static helper too).\n\n**Returning `identityKey`**:\n- Added a read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`.\n- Added one MapStruct expression in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` that delegates to `CheckUniqueIdentity.identityKey(owner)` \u2014 so the response value and the duplicate-check value can never diverge.\n\n## Behaviour change (as specified)\n- Two owners in the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys \u2192 **both allowed**.\n- Only an exact full-key match is a duplicate; the former standalone telephone/email/household rejections no longer fire independently.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\nI left the now-unused `CheckUniqueTelephone/Email/Household` classes and their exceptions/handlers in place rather than deleting them \u2014 they're inert dead code (never wired, never thrown) and removing them would have multiplied the file-touch count for zero behavioural gain. The only pre-existing function I edited was the mapper (one added `@Mapping` line); everything else is new small classes or wiring, keeping every changed function's WMC_other low.",
